meta {
  name: Post AppView Enroll Backfill
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/app.thesocialwire.appview.enrollSources
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{oauthAccessToken}}
  DPoP: {{dpopProof}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "authorDids": [
      "{{authorDid}}"
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Run after starting Charybdis to backfill recent entries for followed authors before relying on live Jetstream ingestion.
  HTTP 503 can include articlesUpdated: true and sourceFailures after healthy sources commit and counters reconcile. Refresh article pages before presenting partial success; sourceFailures contain only category, kind, hostname, optional HTTP status, and count. When available, unavailablePublicationIds contains sorted, deduplicated canonical RSS IDs for failed subscribed feeds; match exact IDs rather than hostnames before offering unsubscribe. These private IDs encode feed URLs and must not be logged. Infrastructure, PDS, counter, and request cancellation failures omit these fields.
}
